<title>ITALY: Fazio says Waigel's original gold plan was wrong.</title>
<headline>Fazio says Waigel's original gold plan was wrong.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Italy governor Antonio Fazio said German Finance Minister Theo Waigel's original plan to seek a special payout this year from a revaluation of Bundesbank gold reserves was wrong.</p>
<p>&quot;I think Waigel's first proposal was completely wrong...and indeed the German authorities withdrew it,&quot; he told a parliamentary budget committee.</p>
<p>Chancellor Helmut Kohl's government retreated from the controversial plan to reap billions of marks in quick cash profits this year to help Germany qualify for Europe's single currency following opposition from the central bank and parliamentarians from Kohl's party.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
